<title>SWEDEN: BA to raise ex-Nordic cargo capacity-source.</title>
<headline>BA to raise ex-Nordic cargo capacity-source.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways plans to replace two Boeing-757s with 767s in its summer schedule on routes to the Nordic region, an industry source said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 240-seat 767, although not much larger than the 185-seat 757 from the passenger business point-of-view, means a significant change from the cargo side, the source said.</p>
<p>The 767 can carry containers which are compatible with a 747, so at London's Heathrow airport the freight can be quickly moved onto a 747.</p>
<p>&quot;It means an improvement in capacity and also a huge improvement in service,&quot; the source said.</p>
<p>One of the flights was between Oslo and London and the other was from Stockholm to London, the source said. The flights would be more or less daily, the source said.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
